  "text": "Pip shares Mara’s page with the people here in the garden.\n\nHappening often. Less frequent means happening less often.\n\nFollow the gathering here. Help and Pause keep your place.\n\nMara’s page is called The Torn Wing. Grandma has her copy.\n\nThis does not change your draft, chosen ending or picture.\n\nPip can't cross the river yet. The bridge pieces may help.\n\nA memory kept in the garden · Pip stays where you left him\n\nTake the repair rope from Grandma’s maintenance box first.\n\nMara is at the passenger dock until she has finished work.\n\nThe whole draft as Sol wrote it. Its ending is still open.\n\nA space where something is missing or things do not meet.\n\nPip takes the two repair ropes from Grandma’s marked box.\n\nShows a time limit, a nearby place, or who did something.\n\nThe seed grew into a lantern-flower after it was planted.\n\nPut something over the top. Here, put soil over the seed.\n\nPreview a position, then tell Sol to place the same tile.\n\nThe parts of the body where the arms join the upper body.\n\nA responsibility or something a person is expected to do.\n\nA musical instrument played by blowing across an opening.\n\nYou direct Sol’s roof repair · Pip is the material helper\n\nGrandma tells this older garden story. “I” means Grandma.\n\nPip carries Grandma’s copy to Mara at the passenger dock.\n\nYou direct Sol’s roof repair; Pip waits beside the ladder\n\nKeep something in your hands or in a particular position.\n\nSol wrote this draft about today’s repair. “I” means Sol.\n\nPip kept his promise. The new lantern-flower is growing.\n\nMara listens while Pip reads her story to the gathering.\n\nStay on the dock path between the boy and Mara’s office.\n\nMara’s story has been shared here. This flower keeps the\n\nThe original manuscript and the exact ending Sol shared.",
